   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PREPARATION OF NATIONAL INVENTORIES OF BANKS OF USED OR UNWANTED CONTROLLED SUBSTANCES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Republic of Togo is undertaking a project to develop a comprehensive national inventory and action plan to strengthen the management of ozone depleting substance (ODS) banks. This will support Togo&apos;s obligations under the Montreal Protocol to phase-out ODS in line with the agreed schedule.  The project will involve extensive data collection and analysis to quantify ODS stocks currently contained in equipment, installations, products, reserves, and waste across different sectors. Comprehensive industry and stakeholder consultations will be conducted to verify data and engage government, importers, service technicians, and waste managers.  The inventory findings will inform a tailored action plan to ensure Togo can manage and destroy ODS banks in an environmentally sustainable manner, in line with international standards and best practices. This includes examining recycling, reclamation and economic feasibility of sound ODS waste management infrastructure.  Overall, the project will build Togo&apos;s capacity and expertise to fulfill its Montreal Protocol commitments. Reducing ODS banks will generate major environmental benefits by averting direct greenhouse gas and ozone depleting emissions.</narrative>
  </description>
